  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Figure 14, 'How digital signatures work', under the heading Document Signing. A signer starts from a document (vaccination data); a hash is calculated from the document, giving the document hash; the hash is digitally signed with a private key, giving the signed hash; the signed hash is added to the document, giving a document with a digitally signed hash (the DDCC:VS).",
